@chapter Crate @code{gpui-ui-kit-macros}
@cindex gpui-ui-kit-macros

@code{gpui-ui-kit-macros} ships the procedural macros used by
@ref{gpui-ui-kit Manual}. There is exactly one macro:
@code{#[derive(ComponentTheme)]}.

@menu
* gpui-ui-kit-macros User Guide::
* gpui-ui-kit-macros Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node gpui-ui-kit-macros User Guide
@section User Guide

End users never use this crate. Component themes derived with it just
"do the right thing" when the global theme changes.

@node gpui-ui-kit-macros Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading What the derive generates

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{impl Default for MyComponentTheme} using the @code{default}
  attribute on each field.
@item @code{impl From<&Theme> for MyComponentTheme} mapping each field
  to a global theme token via the @code{from} attribute.
@end itemize

@subheading Example

@example
use gpui_ui_kit_macros::ComponentTheme;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, ComponentTheme)]
pub struct MyComponentTheme @{
    #[theme(default = 0x007acc, from = accent)]
    pub primary_color: Rgba,

    #[theme(default = 0xffffff, from = text_primary)]
    pub text_color: Rgba,

    #[theme(default = 1.0, from = none)]
    pub opacity: f32,
@}
@end example

@subheading Attribute reference

@table @code
@item default = HEX or LITERAL
Value used in @code{Default::default}.
@item from = TOKEN
Token name in @code{&Theme}. Use @code{none} to keep the default.
@end table

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p gpui-ui-kit-macros
@end example
